# The client needs no build-time environment variables.
#
# The API client uses a relative base URL ("/api"), so requests always go to
# whichever origin served the app:
#
#   local dev              Vite dev server proxies /api -> http://localhost:3001
#   Compose (full profile) nginx proxies /api -> the server container
#   AWS                    the ALB routes /api/* to the backend target group
#
# Keeping the app and API same-origin in every environment means no CORS
# configuration, and no image rebuild needed to change the API address.
